# Magic UI UX MCP Defaults

When working on UI, UX, layout, visual polish, accessibility, or interaction improvements in this project:

- Use the installed Magic UI UX MCP as the primary assistant for design exploration and quality improvements.
- Prioritize user experience outcomes: clarity, hierarchy, accessibility, responsiveness, and consistency.
- Propose concrete design refinements before or alongside implementation when requirements are vague.
- Keep components production-ready and avoid generic-looking UI output.
- Ensure improvements align with the existing product style and branding direction.

If a request is unrelated to frontend design/UX, proceed normally without forcing MCP usage.
